# Git commit message language

When generating Git commit messages for this repository:
- Always write the subject and body in Simplified Chinese, even if previous commits are in English.
- Keep code identifiers, file paths, commands, and proper names in their original form.
- If using Conventional Commits, keep the type and scope unchanged and write the description in Simplified Chinese.
- Return only the commit message, without explanations or Markdown code fences.
